SARP AI Pro
EXECUTABLE FILE INTEGRITY VERIFICATION
SHA-512 CHECKSUM

This document explains how to verify the downloaded SARP AI Pro executable
before running or installing it.

Release file:
SARPAI.exe

Hash algorithm:
SHA-512

Published checksum:
3EF2A4FEFC66160CC471BF6A554FCA33A5722E1D524339214F20D131A692A3B7254FFD590C7E0474B988AEFC8C19CB16B6BF4DFF506330802F15AD889719FFED


HOW TO VERIFY ON WINDOWS

1. Download SARPAI.exe from the official SARP AI Pro source.
2. Open the folder containing SARPAI.exe.
3. Click the File Explorer address bar, type powershell, and press Enter.
4. Run this command:

   Get-FileHash "C:\SARP\SARPAI.exe" -Algorithm SHA512

5. Compare the complete Hash value returned by Windows with the published
   checksum shown in this document.

TIP: If PowerShell shortens the displayed result, run:

   (Get-FileHash "C:\SARP\SARPAI.exe" -Algorithm SHA512).Hash

This displays the complete 128-character SHA-512 value.

HOW TO READ THE RESULT

- MATCH: If both SHA-512 values are identical, the executable matches the
  published checksum.
- NO MATCH: If the values differ, the executable is not identical to the
  file represented by this checksum. Do not run it as a verified release.
  Download the file again from the official SARP AI Pro source and check it
  once more.

IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTE

A matching SHA-512 checksum confirms that the downloaded executable matches
the published checksum. It does not, by itself, prove the identity of the
publisher or guarantee that the software is safe. For stronger publisher
verification, the executable should also be digitally signed with a trusted
code-signing certificate.

Product:
SARP AI Pro
Digital Intelligence System for Higher Education

Keep this document with the executable release. Whenever SARPAI.exe is
updated or replaced, calculate and publish a new SHA-512 checksum.
